### ============================================================
### Auth Rosetta - API tests
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
###
### How to use:
###   1. Start the backend and set @baseUrl for the stack under test.
###   2. Run the requests top to bottom (click "Send Request" above each one).
###   3. At step 4, paste the secret into an authenticator app, then put the
###      current 6-digit code into @code. Codes last 30 seconds, so update
###      @code right before steps 4 and 8.
###   4. To re-run the whole flow, change @email (register returns 409 otherwise).
### ============================================================

# Backend ports: .NET 5001 | NestJS 5002 | Python 5003 | Go 5004 | Java 5005
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5001
@email = test@example.com
@password = Sup3rSecret!
@code = 000000


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 0. VALIDATION (no state is created)
### ------------------------------------------------------------

### 0a. Register with a short password -> expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "short"
}

### 0b. Register with an empty email -> expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. REGISTER -> expect 201 with { otpauthUri, secret }
### Copy the "secret" into your authenticator app (manual entry),
### or paste the otpauthUri into a QR generator.
### ------------------------------------------------------------

# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 1b. Register the same email again -> expect 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. LOGIN BEFORE 2FA IS CONFIRMED -> expect 401
### Even with a correct password and a valid code, login must fail
### because 2FA is not enabled yet.
### ------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. CONFIRM 2FA WITH A WRONG CODE -> expect 400
### ------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/2fa/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "111111"
}

### 3b. Confirm 2FA for an unknown email -> expect 400 (same as a wrong code)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/2fa/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. CONFIRM 2FA WITH A VALID CODE -> expect 200
### Update @code at the top first.
### ------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/2fa/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. LOGIN FAILURES - all three must return an identical 401
### ------------------------------------------------------------

### 5a. Wrong password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "WrongPassword123",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}

### 5b. Wrong code
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "code": "111111"
}

### 5c. Unknown email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. SUCCESSFUL LOGIN -> expect 200 with { token }
### Update @code at the top if the previous one is older than 30 seconds.
### ------------------------------------------------------------

# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. ME
### ------------------------------------------------------------

### 7a. With the token -> expect 200 with { email }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 7b. Without a token -> expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 7c. With a garbage token -> expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token


### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. LOGOUT -> expect 204
### ------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 8b. Same token on /me after logout -> expect 401 (token revoked)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 8c. Logout again with the revoked token -> expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
